WEBVTT

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:12.260
- Thank you for waiting.
- Thank you.

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:21.820
<i>Oh! Why did I call Yamashiro? I don't have any recollection of this.</i>

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.910
<i>Did I get drunk and hit him? Did I do something to him?</i>

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:32.420
- Um, Master.
- Oh, I have to read the newspaper!

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:36.050
Oh, man that horse came through again. I missed it again.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.400
Welcome.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:47.810
Oh, it's full. Do you mind sharing a seat?

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.230
No, I don't.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.120
Please, this way.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.760
Excuse me...May I get some sa-

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:52.190
Amagigoe

00:02:53.410 --> 00:02:59.170
- OK, sure thing. Rice balls, right?
- More to buy?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:04.460
Yea, the Master spilled something on Yamashiro-san's clothes.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:09.340
She wants to make something for him as a sign of apology.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:14.660
I can't believe her. So, what kind of dish are we making?

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:19.430
We're going to make... I forget what the dish is called.

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:24.210
- Can you tell me what kind of dish it is?
- I sure will.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:28.030
It's a dish that's given comfort to many for ages.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.940
It is round and cute, though it has an air of dignity in its shape.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.160
The contrasting white and black colors leave an impression.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:39.500
Wow, what a dish that captures the heart.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:44.600
- Do you know of such a dish?
- Of course I do.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:57.150
Was Yamashiro-san OK?

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:03.680
He'll drop off his shirt at the cleaners. He said to take care of Josephine in the meantime.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:07.530
And where's the person that's at fault for this?

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:12.180
- Wha---at! Where is it?
- What?

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.840
- This! 
 - Ceramic artist of tragedy...

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:20.500
...Kobayashi John. His first exhibition?

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:25.770
- I didn't know you liked ceramics, Master.
- Oh, I'm interested in this!

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.360
What? The lost, matching tea cups?

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:36.080
- Lost?
- The cup that this guy Kobayashi made...

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.010
...the smaller one, got lost during the war.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:47.100
- Oh, it's a matching set?!
- Wow, I can't believe the price of just one of these!?

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:52.070
Oh, look at this. If you find the missing cup, you get...

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:55.980
1, 10, 100, 1000, 10000...

00:04:56.180 --> 00:05:01.300
- You get one million yen?
- You're missing a zero, Arashi-san.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:02.390
What?

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:07.290
10 million yen?! 10 million yen to the one that finds it?
- 10 million yen?!

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.290
- Oh, no!
- What?

00:05:12.990 --> 00:05:16.180
I used it three days ago. That tea cup.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.260
And I might have lost it.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:22.360
Wha---t!

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.560
What do you mean?!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:29.530
I don't know why, but I found one of the cups lying around in the shop.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:35.040
- Why would such a cup be here?!
- I don't know! I don't know why, but it was definitely here.

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:40.960
- It might be fake.
- Um. I think it was authentic. "Kobayashi" was inscribed at the bottom.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.780
- For real?!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:47.420
Arashi-san, wasn't there a customer by the name of Kobayashi that came here?

00:05:48.580 --> 00:05:54.050
Right! Arashi-san would know. She was at "Hakobune" 60 years ago.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:58.610
Hayashi---Kobayashi---Oobayashi...

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:04.850
- I forget the size, but I think he was here.
- Told you! It's real then!

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:09.120
Oh, where have you gone, Kobayashi cup?!

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:15.330
What do you mean you don't know where it went? You used it three days ago, right?

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.160
The cup was perfect for my hand...

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:24.250
...and I told someone to place it in the cupboard in the kitchen, but I can't find it.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:33.010
- There are a lot of tea cups here!
- I can't tell which one is Kobayashi-san's.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:36.610
I told you, that tea cup has Kobayashi inscribed on the bottom!

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:44.670
- It was the perfect size for drinking shochu.
- You were drinking from a 10 million yen cup?

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:49.830
All the cups here don't have Kobayashi inscribed on the bottom.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:56.330
- I wonder if someone put it away somewhere.
- Alright, then I'll do it.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:07:02.440
- Do what?
- Don't you know? - No way!

00:07:04.480 --> 00:07:08.880
It's the order from the Master: "Fly back to three days ago and bring me back the Kobayashi cup!"

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:17.100
- How are the cucumbers coming along?
- It's a miracle.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:23.120
The aroma, moisture, and its presence... Nukadokolina is at her best!

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.960
- Wow.
- This is what I was after all this time.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:32.960
- Now we can give Yamashiro-san a treat.
- Yea!

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:41.780
- Alright, first off: Arashi and Hajime!
- OK, we're off!

00:07:43.920 --> 00:07:49.020
- Wow, Arashi-san is excited.
- She likes these types of assignments.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:54.650
- Thanks for waiting.
- This is Yamashiro-san's dinner as our apology?

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.380
It's a dish that's given comfort to many for ages.

00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:03.250
It is round and cute, though it has an air of dignity in its shape.

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:09.630
- The contrasting white and black colors leave an impression.
- Um, it's rice balls right?

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:21.820
- OK, this is good. Can you guys help me?
- With what?

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:27.340
- A mission to grab the tea cup from the Master from three days ago.
- Tea cup?!

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.800
Yes! I'm counting on you!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:35.780
- You guys will go. Right, Jun? 
- What?

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:38.740
- I refuse.
- Kaya-san.

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:44.310
If you bring it back, I'll get you your favorite cake.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:47.340
- I'll be right back!
- Kaya-san!

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:53.710
- Let's go, Jun.
- Wai-wait. - Cake.

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:59.760
Kaya-san was saying "cake" before she flew.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:04.060
- Great, I'm excited. Now...
- What?!

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:09.510
The dog is conveniently outside. Would you like to fly back?

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.700
Are all of you OK?

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.830
Did you bring it back?!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:29.520
- It was impossible. - Why?
- Because you were running away. - What?

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:35.600
- When did I run away.
- No, I'm talking about you in the past.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.070
Why do you have to be so hard to handle?

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:45.280
What, was it that hard?

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:50.700
When we tried to get the cup from you,
 you know what you said?

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:56.310
- "I'm not going to give it to you, it's mine!"
- Oh! I would say that!

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:01.150
Even if it's trash, if someone wants it, she won't give it up.

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:05.350
- It's not going to be easy to convince her.
- Dang it!

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:08.790
If I can fly back in time, I would convince myself to give it back.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:12.300
- Well, you can't!
- Why?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:18.510
- I think I'll listen to something that I would say.
- If you do that, you'll perish.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:24.110
- Why? - You still don't understand it, huh?
- That's the way it is.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:28.700
Anyway, you weren't in a state to negotiate or anything.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:32.710
Was I just wearing my apron?
- Yes.

00:10:33.830 --> 00:10:37.490
Wow, I must have been drunk.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:40.960
- Why were you only wearing your apron?!
- Oh...

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.630
...it's because when I get drunk, I spill, you know?

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:49.370
I learned from that. If I only wear my apron, I won't get my clothes dirty.

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.360
On top of that, I look like I'm wearing a tube top and some shorts, right?

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:58.330
- No, you could tell.
- Yea, you could see everything.

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:02.020
Wait! Now I remember a little bit.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:07.080
I got chased around by everyone for no reason three days ago.

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.270
It was for the Kobayashi cup, huh?

00:11:10.490 --> 00:11:13.770
The alcohol must have circulated more since you ran around.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:18.970
Master, you told me to put it in the cupboard, right?

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.370
Right.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:24.290
- So, you asked someone to put it there?
- Yes.

00:11:24.410 --> 00:11:29.480
- Yea, I asked Yayoi to put it there.
- Me?

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:35.150
- I don't remember it.
- What?! I'm sure that I gave it to Yayoi!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:41.200
Since I liked it a lot, I wanted someone that would take care of it. 
 That's why I chose Yayoi.

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.560
Alright, calm down Yayoi. Try to remember what happened.

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:52.510
Kanako--- I can't remember.

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:57.800
This is confusing. 
Just fly back and get it for me, Yayoi.

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:01.240
I honestly don't remember your asking me.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:05.730
I've asked you before. Anyway, go with Josephine.
- What?

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.130
- No way.
- She flew.

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:19.490
- Y---Yayoi!
- Salt---

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:28.820
- Y---Yayoi!
- What?

00:12:31.880 --> 00:12:33.860
- Yayoi!
- Yes?

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:39.430
- Are you OK? Does it hurt anywhere?
- No, I'm OK.

00:12:40.190 --> 00:12:43.160
I'm surprised, Yayoi-san and the Master went.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:47.970
I can't believe that I can connect with a woman.

00:12:48.030 --> 00:12:53.060
- Am I an immoral person?
- Yayoi, you're not an immoral person.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:58.000
Yayoi-san's make-up must make it easier to fly.

00:12:58.220 --> 00:13:03.290
Found it! The time that we flew back to still has the Kobayashi cup in the cupboard!

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:08.100
- Oh! You did it, Master!
- You didn't bring it back?

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:13.320
We almost came face to face with the master of 3 days ago. I panicked, and we flew back.

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:18.100
I'm not going to mess up this time. We're flying back to the same time, Yayoi!

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:23.640
Wait! You'll bump into yourselves from a moment ago...

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:28.580
- ...and from three days ago, too.
- It's going to be dangerous for Yayoi.

00:13:28.840 --> 00:13:33.100
- What do you want me to do then?
- Then we'll go.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:36.610
Yayoi-san, do you remember what time you flew to three days ago?

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:39.950
I don't remember the exact time...

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:45.430
- ...but there was a sweet aroma in the kitchen.
- Sweet aroma?

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:50.590
Kaya-san, isn't that when you were making pudding?

00:13:51.230 --> 00:13:55.820
That's right, it was three in the afternoon.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.300
Okay! We're going to go there.

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:02.030
What's wrong, Kaya-san?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:06.430
- I just remembered that there's more pudding.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:22.190
The pudding is inside the tea cup? Wow, that's fancy.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:26.080
There weren't enough pudding cups, so...

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.960
- Wait!
- Doesn't that cup look like the Kobayashi cup?!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:36.720
Slowly! It's a soft pudding. You're going to mess up the taste.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:41.400
Oh, OK. It has nothing inscribed on it.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:47.010
- This isn't the Kobayashi cup.
- Put it back slowly too. - OK.

00:14:49.270 --> 00:14:54.050
OK, I'm going to eat it now. 
There's only one left, but let's all share it.

00:14:56.590 --> 00:15:01.240
Hey! What's your problem?! Arashi-san almost disappeared!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:05.070
Sorry, sorry. 
I didn't know that it was going to be that clean.

00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:10.900
- What are you talking about?
- Well I tried to get the cup myself right now.

00:15:11.120 --> 00:15:16.630
- When did you?!
- What do you think she did to me when she chased me?

00:15:16.820 --> 00:15:18.700
- What?
- Kicked the back of my knee.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:24.150
Well it was more like a kick to the back of the head.

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:29.980
Well, I was just trying to play around, but Hajime is so short...

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:35.010
- No, that's not cool!
- When Hajime-chan hit the cupboard and...

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:42.000
...broke a lot of dishes, I called for people to bring me the broom.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:44.150
Arashi-san came...

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:49.850
- ...and we almost bumped into her.
- I guess I was the one calling myself three days ago.

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.720
No wonder I heard that voice before.

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:58.770
- So did you break a bunch of pudding cups then?
- Yea.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:02.820
- No wonder there weren't enough pudding cups.
- Um.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:08.650
- What, Yayoi?! Are you OK? Are you sick because you linked with a weirdo? - Hey!

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:12.760
- I was asked.
- What?

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:17.850
- I remember the master telling me to put the cup in the cupboard.
- I told you!

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:21.610
- You remembered, Yayoi?
- Well, I didn't really remember, but...

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.730
- ...I was just told right now.
- What?

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:28.910
When I was getting the trash bag to collect the broken dishes...

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:33.490
- ...the Master from three days ago told me about the cup.
- Oh, I get it.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:39.200
The Master from back then thought Yayoi-san was from the same time.

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:44.360
That's why the Master remembers and Fushimi-san doesn't.

00:16:44.680 --> 00:16:50.630
- That's why. Anyway, where's the cup?
- I put it back in the cupboard as I was told.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:54.870
What! Why didn't you just bring it back?

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:59.010
- What? You told me to put it back. 
- No, I meant...

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:03.310
Wait, you helped me clean all those dishes...

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:08.760
- ... Yayoi-chan?
- Yes.- I kind of helped too.

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:14.360
Oh, you brought us the newspaper from the back room.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:18.440
- That was you, Master?
- That means...

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:24.560
...that everyone flew back a little too far.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:27.900
Oh! We should fly to a time a little before that then!

00:17:28.030 --> 00:17:33.410
- I'll get it this time! Let's go, Yayoi.
- Wait, if you do that...

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:39.990
...you might bump into yourself from three days ago, a little while ago, and just right now!

00:17:40.390 --> 00:17:44.500
Yayoi might bump into the Yayoi from a few minutes ago, too.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:48.800
No, it's alright. I remember the exact time.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:51.920
We flew to three days ago at 3:17 pm.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:57.240
- Why do you remember the exact time?
- Don't mind it right now.

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:01.760
- So, Hajime and Arashi should go to this time.
- I'm not going to go!

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:08.450
We might bump into Arashi-san from three days ago and a little bit ago.

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:12.840
- What about you, Kanako and Sunglass. 
 - We're not going.

00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:14.290
What about you, Kaya and Jun?

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:20.420
- We're not going. 
-<i>I think the pudding satisfied her sweet tooth. </i>

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:23.040
Alright then!

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:26.670
- Oh, there's Kobayashi Akira!
- What?!

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:40.310
- You were able to bring it back.
- Man, I can't believe you, Master.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.330
Why did you wrap it up so acrobatically?

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:47.000
Your physical ability increased 
when there was a lot of money involved in it.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:52.630
- Are you OK, Yayoi?
- It might be too much. Her body is almost disappearing.

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:59.070
Then what time period should we fly into to get the Kobayashi cup?

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:06.140
- Do you understand what you did, Master?
- All of us almost disappeared from this earth.

00:19:06.590 --> 00:19:09.040
- But!
- MASTER!

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:14.740
Alright, then I'll be quiet.

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:25.120
- Man, I'm tired. Do you guys want some coffee?
- I want some.

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:33.580
<i>Kobayashi</i>

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:43.890
Oh, that's a pretty good scratch. 
It's really in there.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:49.940
It's a really pretty cup, though.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:54.650
- Can I have that cup then?
- Oh, sure.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.020
- What is that?
- It's a baby cucumber.

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:04.080
To lead Nukadokolina to perfection, I'm...

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:09.210
- ...growing my own vegetables.
- Great idea!

00:20:17.780 --> 00:20:21.090
Hey! Your plate has a name written under it too?

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.470
It's just like the Kobayashi cup.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:33.870
Oh, Yamashiro, did you get the racehorse ticket from three days ago?

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:37.780
Right, 8th race 5 -2-7 in a row.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:41.260
8527, "Hakobune," the one that's really easy to remember.

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:46.000
What? Oh, you brought it earlier?

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:49.830
Alright, come back soon, OK? 
We have some great food for you.

00:20:50.780 --> 00:20:55.270
I'm going to get everyone a treat! Wow!

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:34.180
- How are you, Yayoi? 
 - I'm doing well, Kanako.

00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:39.440
- Oh, that's good. 
- I read another great book.

00:22:39.910 --> 00:22:44.720
- What was the book called? 
- It's called...

00:22:44.950 --> 00:22:49.250
- I forget the title. 
- Can you tell me what the story was about?

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:51.410
I sure will.

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:58.770
It was about a very cute and healthy boy and...

00:22:58.990 --> 00:23:02.470
...a girl that loved him dearly.

00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:08.550
Crawling through the darkness and using many tools, they face their enemies.

00:23:08.710 --> 00:23:11.160
Through it, the two learn about true love.

00:23:11.290 --> 00:23:16.610
The boy experiences a transformation, one that shakes the earth, when the girl is in trouble.

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:21.390
- Wow, what a great story. 
- The boy that always carries a piglet with him...

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:25.340
- ....says this phrase. 
- What is it? Can you tell me what that is?

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:29.220
Mako-chan, why do you...

00:23:30.850 --> 00:23:34.860
- When I say pickles... 
- It tastes great when you put a lot of care into it.

00:23:34.860 --> 00:23:39.510
I have other names for it too. 
 - Nukadokochev, Nukadokovic, and Nukadokomach.

